PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- Consensus status: Complete unanimity persists across all 15 colleagues for Choice B (increase, more, Keap1), with no lingering disputes.
- Core mechanism: Treatment of RAW 264.7 macrophages with the 4-HNE alkyne probe covalently modifies Keap1 via Michael addition, stabilizing Nrf2 to increase ARE-driven ALDH expression. Compared to the lipid aldehyde at 50 µM, which triggers proteotoxic stress and translational attenuation, 50 µM 4-OI provides sustained, non-toxic Keap1 alkylation that enables more pronounced de novo ALDH accumulation.
- Final decision: Maintain firm agreement on B.
}

